source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons update -h <==
Update every managed addon on every client, or the ones named (undo with one undo)

Usage: omaddons update [OPTIONS] [ADDON]...
Aliases: upgrade

Arguments:
  [ADDON]...  Only these installed addons (names, or catalog names and aliases); default: all

Options:
      --all                Every managed addon on every selected client (the default)
      --channel <CHANNEL>  Switch the named addons to stable, beta or alpha and install that
                           channel's newest release
      --refresh            Ask every source now, even when it was checked in the last 15 minutes
      --strict             Exit 6 when only some of the addons update
      --no-deps            Update only the named addons, not the ones their TOCs require

Examples:
  omaddons update                every addon on every client
  omaddons update dbm -t retail  one addon on one client
  omaddons update --dry-run      what would change

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons update --help <==
Update every managed addon on every client, or the ones named (undo with one undo)

Usage: omaddons update [OPTIONS] [ADDON]...
Aliases: upgrade

Arguments:
  [ADDON]...
          Only these installed addons (names, or catalog names and aliases); default: all

Options:
      --all
          Every managed addon on every selected client (the default)

      --channel <CHANNEL>
          Switch the named addons to stable, beta or alpha and install that channel's newest release

      --refresh
          Ask every source now, even when it was checked in the last 15 minutes

      --strict
          Exit 6 when only some of the addons update

      --no-deps
          Update only the named addons, not the ones their TOCs require

Examples:
  omaddons update                   every addon on every client; one undo reverts it all
  omaddons update DBM -t retail     one addon on one client
  omaddons update --dry-run         what would change
  omaddons update WeakAuras --channel beta

A given version is an install, which pins it:
  omaddons install <addon> --version V
  omaddons pin <addon> --version V

See also: outdated, pin, undo

Global options:
      --json              One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>   Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>   The client to act on: id, key, game mode (sod and hardcore select the
                          Classic Era client), family, product, flavor folder, path, or all (every
                          client) [alias: --flavor]
      --dry-run           Show the plan without changing anything (ignored by commands that change
                          nothing)
      --actor <ACTOR>     Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>     Why, recorded verbatim in history (at most 200 characters; ignored by
                          commands that change nothing)
      --offline           Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running     Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --if-match <TOKEN>  Change nothing unless the plan is still the one the --dry-run that
                          returned this token (data.precondition) showed
      --no-color          No ANSI color
      --no-progress       No progress output
      --progress <MODE>   Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet             Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...        More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help              Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
